Dear all
While reading one of the latest emails on the forum, i followed a document
pointed out as a reference concerning a study on Bluetooth location. In the
document it says:
 "Although the Bluetooth protocol allows a master to support up to 3
simultaneous SCO links and 7 simultaneous ACL links, typical consumer
hardware only supports a single SCO link and 3 ACL links. Very lightweight
devices such as the current generation of Bluetooth-enabled mobile phones
only support a single SCO and ACL link at a time (which is sufficient to
drive a wireless headset)."
 Is anyone aware of class 1 usb devices wich dont have this limitation.
Meaning that supports the full 7 simultaneous ACL links and the 3
simultaneous SCO links?
 Thank you
 Artur

